    {
      "short": "Front door",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "One address, many servers",
      "body": [
        "A <span class=\"term\">load balancer</span> sits in front, owns the public address, and forwards each request to one of the servers behind it. Readers never learn the servers exist — which means servers can be added or removed freely.",
        "The simplest policy is <span class=\"term\">round robin</span>: 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3… With similar requests and similar servers, each gets a third of the traffic."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Load balancer owns brightpost.io",
        "~ Round robin across 3 servers",
        "~ Biggest share 70% → 33%"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "rps": 3000,
        "p95": 120,
        "errors": 0,
        "healthy": "3 / 3",
        "maxShare": 33
