    {
      "short": "L4 or L7",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "How much does the balancer read?",
      "body": [
        "A <span class=\"term\">Layer 4</span> balancer works on TCP connections: it sees IP addresses and ports and forwards bytes without reading them. It's very fast and works for any protocol, but every request on one connection goes to the same server.",
        "A <span class=\"term\">Layer 7</span> balancer speaks HTTP. It terminates TLS, reads paths, headers and cookies, and can route <code>/api</code> and <code>/images</code> to different pools, retry a failed request, or add headers. More features, more work per request."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "~ Balancer now terminates HTTPS (L7)",
        "+ Comparison card"
      ],
