    {
      "short": "Least conns",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Send work to whoever is least busy",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Least connections</span> sends each request to the server with the fewest requests in flight. A server stuck on exports has more open requests, so new work flows elsewhere automatically.",
        "Variants weigh by server size or measured response time. A cheap alternative is the <span class=\"term\">power of two choices</span>: pick two servers at random, use the less busy one — nearly as good, with far less bookkeeping."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "~ Algorithm: round robin → least connections",
        "~ Exports spread out",
        "~ p95 900 → 210 ms"
      ],
