    {
      "short": "Hashing",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Same reader, same server",
      "body": [
        "Sometimes you <i>want</i> repeat visitors on the same server — say, so each server's in-memory cache stays warm for its readers. <span class=\"term\">Hash-based routing</span> computes <code>hash(reader_id) mod 3</code> and always picks that server.",
        "Two catches: popular readers make shares uneven (41% here), and with plain <i>mod N</i>, adding a fourth server remaps about three-quarters of readers. <span class=\"term\">Consistent hashing</span> limits that reshuffle to roughly 1/N."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Hashing trades even load for locality. Use it when a warm per-server cache or connection is worth more than perfect balance."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Algorithm: hash on reader id",
        "~ Shares now uneven (41 / 33 / 26%)"
      ],
