    {
      "short": "Health checks",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Ask before you send",
      "body": [
        "The balancer now sends a <span class=\"term\">health check</span> — a tiny request such as <code>GET /healthz</code> — to every server every few seconds. After 3 failures in a row it takes a server out of rotation; after 2 successes it puts it back.",
        "Traffic now flows only to servers 1 and 2. Each carries 50% more than before, but errors fall back to almost zero. When server 3 recovers, it rejoins on its own."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Make the health check test what the server really needs (can it reach its database?), but keep it cheap — it runs thousands of times an hour."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Health checks to every server",
        "- Server 3 removed from rotation",
        "~ Errors 33% → ~0%"
      ],
