    {
      "short": "Door twice",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "title": "Who balances the balancer?",
      "body": [
        "Every request now flows through one balancer. If it fails, three healthy servers become unreachable — the front door is the new single point of failure.",
        "So balancers run in pairs. A standby watches the active one with heartbeats and takes over its address — a <span class=\"term\">floating IP</span> — within seconds. Managed cloud balancers do this for you across several zones."
